# The repo currently stores LF because core.autocrlf=true on the Windows dev box
# normalises on commit. That is a machine setting, not a repo guarantee — flip it and
# the next commit ships CRLF. A shell script with CRLF fails on the VPS with the
# famously unhelpful "\r: command not found", and a systemd unit with CRLF fails to
# parse. Pin the ones that must be LF regardless of who commits them.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
